theory.intro:
Inside a quadrant, the sign of a trigonometric ratio depends only on the quadrant the angle lies in. **ASTC** records which ratios are positive: reading anticlockwise from Q1 it spells **A**ll, **S**in, **T**an, **C**os.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.6,0)--(2.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-2.6)--(0,2.6) node[above] {$y$};
\node[font=\Large] at (1.3,1.3) {$\mathbf{A}$};
\node[font=\Large] at (-1.3,1.3) {$\mathbf{S}$};
\node[font=\Large] at (-1.3,-1.3) {$\mathbf{T}$};
\node[font=\Large] at (1.3,-1.3) {$\mathbf{C}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
